## Errors & Mistakes
My first summary of the working tree missed that `hooks` had been emptied
and that `extraKnownMarketplaces` was dropped. I reported only the model
churn. Both losses were only caught when I diffed HEAD against the
worktree directly instead of reading the summarized `git diff` output.
Lesson: the diff-rendering tool elides context lines, so a deleted key can
look like unchanged context. Read whole files when auditing config.

## Dead Ends
Briefly restored both `hooks` and `extraKnownMarketplaces` into the file
before the user said to remove them. That restoration was reverted in this
same commit, so it never landed in history.

## Hints for Future Agents
- claude_settings.json is a SYMLINK TARGET: ~/.claude/settings.json points
  at it. Claude Code rewrites it live. It changed under me twice during
  this session (effortLevel went xhigh -> medium -> low, voice keys
  appeared then were removed). Always re-read before staging.
- rtk was installed from git+https://github.com/rtk-ai/rtk at v0.42.2, not
  from crates.io. Reinstalling needs the git URL.
- The wakatime plugin supplies its own hooks from
  ~/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/wakatime/hooks/hooks.json. Deleting the
  `hooks` key here does not affect it.

